<Project>

  <!--
    Repository-wide build settings.

    The test suite drives Microsoft PowerPoint over COM to render slides.
    PowerPoint is single-instance, so two test processes cannot render at the
    same time. `dotnet test` runs a multi-target project's target frameworks
    in parallel unless told otherwise, which put multiple processes in
    contention and made the COM render self-tests fail intermittently while
    they queued rather than while they rendered. Visio page rendering now
    uses the fully managed CanvasNet.Vsdx library (no COM), so it does not
    contribute to this contention, but the suite stays serialized because
    PowerPoint COM still does.

    TestTfmsInParallel is the SDK's own control for this; see
    Microsoft.TestPlatform.CrossTargeting.targets, which resolves it as
    ValueOrDefault(TestTfmsInParallel, BuildInParallel). Combined with
    maxParallelThreads=1 in each test project's xunit.runner.json, exactly one test
    runs at a time across the whole suite. That is slower, and deliberately so: the
    contention was never in the product, only in how the suite exercised it.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TestTfmsInParallel>false</TestTfmsInParallel>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
